From c0ebbab1db20a5a6d638012eb4611118cbed83c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:47:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-lge-joan: fix micbias levels,
 ground switch and AMIC4

Three separate defects in joan's codec node, all found by decompiling the
stock LG device tree out of the DTBs appended to the retail boot.img.

1. Micbias levels were never measured.  All four rails carried
   qcom,micbiasN-microvolt = <1800000>, which is wcd-common.c's
   WCD_DEF_MICBIAS_MV fallback.  Stock has

     qcom,cdc-micbias1-mv = <0xabe>   2750 mV
     qcom,cdc-micbias2-mv = <0x7d0>   2000 mV
     qcom,cdc-micbias3-mv = <0xabe>   2750 mV
     qcom,cdc-micbias4-mv = <0xabe>   2750 mV

   Underbiasing costs analog mic sensitivity, and MICBIAS2 is worse than
   that: wcd934x uses common.micb_mv[1] as cfg->micb_mv, so MBHC's
   jack-type and button comparator maths scale with it.

2. The ground jack switch was left at mainline's default.  Stock sets
   qcom,msm-mbhc-gnd-swh = <0>, and Qualcomm's encoding is 1 = normally
   open, 0 = normally closed, so this needs
   qcom,ground-jack-type-normally-closed.  Without it, gnd_swh stays true
   and wcd_mbhc_init() writes the wrong value into
   WCD_MBHC_GND_PLUG_TYPE.  The comment added when the button thresholds
   first landed had this mapping inverted -- it described hphl-swh = <1>
   as "NC" -- and noted that the live jack IRQ was still dead; a wrong
   ground plug type is a plausible cause of that and is worth retesting.

3. The "AMIC4", "MIC BIAS4" route was missing.  joan has three built-in
   analog mics, not two: LG's factory test path mictest-allmic captures
   ADC1, ADC2, ADC3 and ADC4 together, and the camcorder paths use
   ADC1+ADC3+ADC4 with the ADC1/ADC3 assignment swapped by device
   orientation.  Deliberately still no DMIC routes -- every
   "dmic-endfire" named path in the stock mixer_paths_tavil.xml resolves
   to analog mics, and the one path that really does select a digital mic
   (speaker-mic-liquid) targets Qualcomm's Liquid reference board.

All ten board revisions LG ships (qcom,board-id 0x308..0xf08, one
qcom,msm-id) agree on every audio and MBHC property, so none of this is
revision- or model-specific; the only per-revision deltas in those DTBs
are battery, charging, USB-C SBU select and the Quad DAC internal LDO.

Every property used here is already documented in qcom,wcd934x.yaml,
whose own example carries the same threshold values.  DTB builds clean.

Not yet booted; micbias levels, ground switch polarity and in-line button
decode all still need hardware confirmation.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-lge-joan.dts | 68 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-lge-joan.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-lge-joan.dts
index 07c42aa34baf..ae1eee45d3b5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-lge-joan.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-lge-joan.dts
@@ -1147,25 +1147,54 @@ wcd9340: codec@1,0 {
 			pinctrl-0 = <&wcd_intr_default>;
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 
-			qcom,micbias1-microvolt = <1800000>;
-			qcom,micbias2-microvolt = <1800000>;
-			qcom,micbias3-microvolt = <1800000>;
-			qcom,micbias4-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			/*
+			 * Micbias levels read out of the stock LG device tree,
+			 * decompiled from the DTBs appended to the retail
+			 * boot.img (qcom,cdc-micbiasN-mv, in mV): MICBIAS1/3/4
+			 * = 0xabe = 2750, MICBIAS2 = 0x7d0 = 2000.  All ten
+			 * board revisions LG ships agree on these.
+			 *
+			 * These were previously all 1800000, which is
+			 * wcd-common.c's WCD_DEF_MICBIAS_MV fallback rather than
+			 * a measured value; it underbiases the analog mics.
+			 * MICBIAS2 additionally feeds MBHC -- wcd934x uses
+			 * common.micb_mv[1] as cfg->micb_mv -- so a wrong value
+			 * skews the jack-type and button comparator maths too.
+			 */
+			qcom,micbias1-microvolt = <2750000>;
+			qcom,micbias2-microvolt = <2000000>;
+			qcom,micbias3-microvolt = <2750000>;
+			qcom,micbias4-microvolt = <2750000>;
 
 			/*
-			 * Without button thresholds, wcd_mbhc_init logs
-			 * "missing qcom,mbhc-buttons-vthreshold-microvolt"
-			 * and never arms jack detect.
+			 * Headset (MBHC) jack detection and in-line remote.
+			 * The jack is qcom,mbhc-audio-jack-type = "4-pole-jack"
+			 * downstream, i.e. it carries a mic and a remote.
+			 *
+			 * Switch types, from the stock DTB:
+			 *   qcom,msm-mbhc-hphl-swh = <1>  normally open
+			 *   qcom,msm-mbhc-gnd-swh  = <0>  normally closed
 			 *
-			 * Downstream qcom,msm-mbhc-hphl-swh = <1> is NC.
-			 * On joan, that property left removal stuck [on].
-			 * Omit qcom,hphl-jack-type-normally-closed so
-			 * hphl_swh defaults true (NO). Boot-unplugged is
-			 * then [off]; live jack IRQ is still dead.
+			 * Qualcomm's encoding is 1 = normally open, 0 = normally
+			 * closed, so HPHL wants mainline's default (property
+			 * absent leaves hphl_swh true) and ground needs telling
+			 * explicitly.  An earlier revision of this node had that
+			 * mapping inverted in a comment and left gnd_swh at its
+			 * default true, which writes the wrong value into
+			 * WCD_MBHC_GND_PLUG_TYPE; that is a candidate cause of
+			 * the live insert/remove IRQ never behaving.
+			 *
+			 * Without the button ladder, wcd_dt_parse_mbhc_data()
+			 * defaults btn_high[0..7] to 500000, so every button on
+			 * an in-line remote compares equal and decodes as BTN_0.
+			 * 75/150/237 mV is the standard Qualcomm ladder and what
+			 * qcom,wcd934x.yaml documents.
 			 */
+			qcom,ground-jack-type-normally-closed;
 			qcom,mbhc-headset-vthreshold-microvolt = <1700000>;
 			qcom,mbhc-headphone-vthreshold-microvolt = <50000>;
-			qcom,mbhc-buttons-vthreshold-microvolt = <75000 150000 237000 500000 500000 500000 500000 500000>;
+			qcom,mbhc-buttons-vthreshold-microvolt = <75000 150000 237000 500000
+								 500000 500000 500000 500000>;
 
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
@@ -1275,11 +1304,22 @@ sound {
 		 * SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT endpoints and need no board route to be
 		 * usable; they are reached by the RX INTn chain kcontrols.
 		 */
+		/*
+		 * joan has three built-in analog mics plus the headset mic; LG's
+		 * own factory test path ("mictest-allmic" in the stock
+		 * mixer_paths_tavil.xml) captures ADC1, ADC2, ADC3 and ADC4
+		 * together, and the camcorder paths use ADC1+ADC3+ADC4.  Every
+		 * "dmic-endfire" named path in that file resolves to analog mics
+		 * as well, so no digital mic is populated on this board and no
+		 * DMIC route belongs here.  AMIC4 reaches ADC4 through the
+		 * codec's AMIC4_5 SEL mux.
+		 */
 		audio-routing =
 			"RX_BIAS", "MCLK",
 			"AMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
 			"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
-			"AMIC3", "MIC BIAS3";
+			"AMIC3", "MIC BIAS3",
+			"AMIC4", "MIC BIAS4";
 
 		mm1-dai-link {
 			link-name = "MultiMedia1";
